+## Note attachments from the phone (QR `target`)
+
+The invoice QR payload (`mode=app`) has a `target` field:
+- `invoice` (default): scan opens the invoice for document uploads, as before.
+- `note`: scan focuses the invoice, opens its Notes sheet and asks for files. The files are saved as a new note with attachments.
+
+The web page shows this QR in the **Note QR** button on the Notes & comments card. Mobile API for the save: `POST /api/v1/invoices/<serial>/notes?batch_id=` (multipart `file` or `files`, optional `body`, requires `notes.create`).
+
+## Live link lookup and background forms
+
+- `GET /invoices/link-lookup?batch_id=&serial=&current=` returns `{found, invoice:{serial_number,date,book,page,total_amount,amounts,batch_name,...}}` or `{found:false, message}`. Only invoices the user may access are returned.
+- The link form and the note form submit in the background (`data-history-form`): typed text is kept, the form clears on success, and the Linked invoices / Notes lists refresh in place (`data-live-region data-live-allow-forms`).
+
